Detect arg-count mismatches in algebra/populate

Thread `errors: &mut Vec<CompileError>` through `walk_rule` and its
helpers. `walk_pred_atom` and `emit_app` push
`PredicateArgumentNumber`/`FunctionArgumentNumber` onto it whenever a
resolved pred or func disagrees on argument count. Resolution of member
preds/funcs depends on type info that propagates over the populate/close
fixed point, so re-walks can flip a previously unresolvable site into a
checked one. `build_structures` resets the Vec at the start of each
iteration and uses the final-iteration Vec as the ground truth, then
appends it to the conflict-derived errors.

Stop iterating `pred_arg_num_should_match` /
`func_arg_num_should_match` from `semantics::check_eqlog`; the
eqlog-side rules and predicates remain defined in eqlog.eql but no
longer feed compile errors. Drop the `nat`/`nats` helpers in
`eqlog_util`, which were only consumed by the removed iterators.
